  "name": null,
  "problem": "A speedboat travels downstream on a river. The table below gives the speed $v(t)$, in miles per hour, of the boat at certain moments during its journey.\n\n| $t\\,(\\text{hours})$ | $0$ | $0.5$ | $1$ | $1.5$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $v(t)\\,(\\text{mi/hour})$ | $10$ | $35$ | $40$ | $65$ | $80$ |\n\nUse a left Riemann sum for $v(t)$ over the interval $[0,2]$ with four subintervals to approximate the total distance traveled by the speedboat.\n\n*Hint: The distance traveled is given by the area under the speed-time graph.*",
  "worked_solution": "",
